\title{A Transformation-Semigroup Theory of the Magma Monoid}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{11 August 2026}

\begin{abstract}
Let $X$ be a set and let $\Bin(X)$ denote the set of all binary operations
$f : X \times X \to X$, equipped with the associative product
$(f * g)(a,b) = g(f(a,b), f(b,a))$, introduced by H.~S.~Kim and J.~Neggers.
We develop a complete transformation-semigroup theory of this monoid. The
central device is the \emph{unfolding} $f \mapsto \widehat f$,
$\widehat f(a,b) = (f(a,b), f(b,a))$, which converts $*$ into composition and
identifies $\Bin(X)$, anti-isomorphically, with the centralizer of the reversal
involution $\sigma(a,b) = (b,a)$ in the full transformation monoid of
$X \times X$. From this identification we obtain: a complete characterization
of von Neumann regular elements ($f$ is regular if and only if every
commutative value $f(x,y) = f(y,x)$ is attained on the diagonal as some
$f(z,z)$), and hence the failure of $\Bin(X)$ to be a regular monoid for
$|X| \ge 2$; criteria for left and right divisibility and for Green's relations
$\mathcal{L}, \mathcal{R}, \mathcal{H}, \mathcal{D}$, together with the fact
that regularity is a $\mathcal{D}$-class invariant; the computation of the
centre, $Z(\Bin(X)) = \{\ell, r\} \cong \Zm/2$ for $|X| \ge 2$; the
identification of the unit group with the centralizer of reversal in
$\Sym(X \times X)$ and the exact order $n!\,2^{m}\,m!$, $m = \binom n2$, for
$|X| = n$; a generalization of the regularity criterion to an arbitrary group
action, in which regularity is governed by stabilizers; and tropical
applications, where the commutative idempotent operations form a left-zero band
inside a single $\mathcal{L}$-class, while tropical multiplication is regular
exactly when the value monoid is $2$-divisible.
\end{abstract}

